sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila grimshawi Turing wavelength at 2.8 µm (detail) — MorphoEval overall 85.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 of loop 3186. Schnakenberg kinetics with δ = D_v/D_u = 16.3186 place the fastest-growing mode at 2.766 µm (slot anchor 2.765e-06 m, Holocene 0 Ma). A cosine-seeded integration matches the exponential growth law at Pearson r = 0.99974. The same kinetics at the predecessor (δ = 10.40, λ = 2.512 µm) and successor (δ = 12.85, λ = 2.629 µm) keep grimshawi as the longest detail-scale wavelength. The animation is a two-arm spiral at that wavenumber, radially enveloped by the gallery specimen. Equal diffusion gives σ_max = -0.717. Not yet in this pass: a plotted continuous δ sweep, an orientation-histogram KS, an Otsu foreground comparison, and a rendered ablation whose image-fitness drop is measured. Overall 85.5/100 (faithfulness 85.1, reproducibility 86.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 87, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 87. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 562825 B, 1248×960 px, artifact_sha256 d07038e2dddcbb919c4840deffc543970092787bdff1e6b4f5fd45bdbba0d789 (sha256 d07038e2dddcbb919c4840deffc543970092787bdff1e6b4f5fd45bdbba0d789), spec_fingerprint e889fa230e849b3a3849aace67edfdc63e0c1f6e6b4678385e1b298ef5811b4a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e889fa230e849b3a3849aace67edfdc63e0c1f6e6b4678385e1b298ef5811b4a; artifact_sha256: d07038e2dddcbb919c4840deffc543970092787bdff1e6b4f5fd45bdbba0d789; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=ac4d59314c82a9c0..., datasets/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=4ea3740942a29423..., datasets/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=ebf2b96514b75c28...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Schnakenberg (1979) supply the instability and the activator-inhibitor kinetics. | Edwards et al. (2007) document Hawaiian picture-wing diversity including D. grimshawi. Werner et al. (2010) show D. guttifera spots are Wingless-driven. Neither paper reports a 2.765 µm wavenumber.; reconstructed_in_script: δ-dependent fastest mode, numerical growth-rate fit, and the chronoseries order ficusphila < guttifera < grimshawi at fixed D_u. | Spiral-wave render calibrated to the gallery asset's radial luminance envelope and melanin colour regression.; transfer_boundary: The gallery frame is a project spiral asset, not a 2.8 µm micrograph. Wikimedia hits were envelope labels and were not used as the target.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Edwards or Werner measured this wavelength. | Does not claim the saturated nonlinear Schnakenberg spot field stays at 2.765 µm; the reported law is the linear fastest mode. | Does not claim the 199 µm grimshawi primordium slot.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Plot the continuous δ sweep (λ versus δ) on the comparison figure so parameter expressivity is visible, not only asserted.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add an orientation-histogram KS statistic and an Otsu foreground-fraction comparison between the specimen mask and the rendered equilibrium.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Render an ablation (equal diffusion or zero-arm carrier) and record the drop in specimen CV relative to the Turing spiral.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.855"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, loop 3186 pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

